  "notes": "Cash-basis city (modified cash; proprietary funds report capital assets and debt), FYE 9/30/23. Governmental lines from p4 Total Governmental column (General + Bond); transfers printed inside the receipt/disbursement totals recorded in transfers_in/out with includes (General out 25,996 + Bond out 85,995 = 111,991; in 3,829; net 108,162 = proprietary transfers in). Taxes 778,658 split by the fund schedules' printed rows (GF property 277,957, sales 293,537, franchise 29,164 on p8; Bond Fund taxes 178,000 = property tax from the p2 Statement of Activities, which prints Property 455,956). Intergovernmental revenues 286,958 kept as one line (p8 breakdown adds to 286,959). Debt service 82,945 split per Bond Fund schedule p9 (principal 66,250, interest 14,218, bond fees 880, county commissions 1,597). Business-type from p6 proprietary statement of revenues, expenses and changes in net position (same measurement as the p2 Statement of Activities: expenses 619,934 tie; p2 charges 712,168 = p6 revenues incl. interest and transfers less the Water 'Other' 23,864 shown as Other income), measure net position; budgetary-basis Line of credit 189,000 appears only in the p10 schedule (receipt line, Loan Proceeds) and p7 cash flows. Cash is printed only as separate lines (no total), so beginning/ending cash are null; fund balances from p4. Balance sheet: governmental lines from p3 (totals equal p1 governmental column), business-type from p1 with debt split by due date from p5. Detail: General Fund p8, Bond Fund p9, Proprietary Funds p10 (single combined column). Read pages 1-10 of 10"
